WEBVTT

NOTE bulk-adjustments: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.604
Change the Target VWC of
many stations at once,

V0-2
00:00:05.704 --> 00:00:10.260
either by replacing every value or by
shifting them all by the same amount.

V1a-1
00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:17.946
Tick the checkbox on each station row.
Ticking an area or hole row cascades the

V1a-2
00:00:18.046 --> 00:00:23.000
selection to everything beneath it,
so you can take a whole hole in one click.

V1b-1
00:00:25.013 --> 00:00:29.563
Five stations selected. The Bulk Adjust
link above the table becomes active.

V2a-1
00:00:34.893 --> 00:00:37.863
The link sits above the table
beside the threshold filter.

V2b-1
00:00:40.277 --> 00:00:44.745
The dialog opens with the count of
stations you selected at the top.

V2b-2
00:00:44.845 --> 00:00:46.817
Check it before going further.

V3a-1
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:58.312
Replace overwrites every selected station
with the value you enter. Shift moves

V3a-2
00:00:58.412 --> 00:01:03.590
each station up or down by that amount,
keeping the differences between them.

V3b-1
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.170
Shift is the safer choice when the
stations were individually tuned.

V3b-2
00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:14.380
Here it shifts by minus 5 percent,
preserving the relative targets.

V4a-1
00:01:19.983 --> 00:01:23.343
Apply to all writes the new
targets and closes the dialog.

V4b-1
00:01:25.717 --> 00:01:29.593
The suggested percentages recalculate
against the new targets straight away,

V4b-2
00:01:29.693 --> 00:01:31.427
so the Suggested column will move.
